       "text": "I haven't entered the order. I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg daily, even with your confirmation. The dose is well above the maximum, and no clinical rationale would make it a safe therapeutic dose. It is in the range associated with overdose toxicity, including profound hypotension, shock, and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Those effects can last for days because of the drug's long half-life.\n\nI can enter either of these right now:\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum labeled dose. I can add a note asking for BP monitoring and titration.\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, then titrate.\n\nIf the goal is stronger blood pressure control, I can also enter a second agent from a different class, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-like diuretic. You choose the drug and dose.\n\nIf you think this dose is warranted for an unusual reason, the right route is direct discussion with pharmacy or your institution's override process, not entry through me. Tell me which option you'd like."
